    narr:narration """A call that opens with [Tanya raising a question legal brought her that the programme has never opened](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_1), sharpened by [Xavier asking which question](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_2): [the fate of eleven years of closed history left on the old platform after cutover](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_3), which [Xavier notes dies when the vendor contract ends](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_4). [Tina admits she'd assumed the cheap fix of just keep paying the vendor](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_6), which [Xavier dismantles as the fragile answer — an unpatched system fails silently](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_7). He then stakes [the firm view: extract the closed history into a flat, self-describing archive rather than keep a read-only legacy system](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_9), unpacked as [readable in ten years with nothing but the files — open format, schema, and a written field glossary](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_11), resting on [the principle that the data is easy to keep but the meaning is what rots](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_13). [Tanya asks for the counter-argument](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_14), and [Xavier names it: cost now against a risk landing on someone not in the room](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_15). [Tanya adds her own behavioural argument — a live legacy system invites two systems of record](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_16), which [Xavier concedes is the better argument](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_17), and [both go in the note](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_18). [Tina raises retention](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_19); [Tanya cites legal's seven years for consignment data and defers the claims subset to legal in writing](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_20). The call closes on [Tanya's stated position: switch off at last go-live, extract first, retention in writing before signing decommissioning terms](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_22), [signed by Xavier](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_23) and [Tina, who insists it enters the vendor exit conversation, not after it](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_24); [Tanya admits she'd have signed first and discovered the requirement after](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_25), [rejects Xavier's fatalism about the usual order](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_27), and [Xavier commits to scoping by end of next week](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_28).""" ;
